WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.160
Let’s say you’re trying to
find some solid information

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.620
about a serious health
problem that concerns you,

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:08.320
like high blood pressure,
or diabetes.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.920
Yet, everywhere you look,

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.640
someone’s trying to sell you
something like vitamins,

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.920
yoga mats, blenders, drugs.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.560
Well, breathe a
sigh of relief

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.640
because all we bring
you are the facts.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.040
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.520
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.000
When accompanied by a
strength-training regimen,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.640
3 grams of creatine a day may improve
muscle performance in older adults.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.080
Here’s our first story.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.840
Creatine is a compound formed
naturally in the human body

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.040
that is primarily involved
in energy production

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:43.800
in our muscles and brain.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.840
It’s also naturally formed
in the bodies of many animals we eat,

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.520
and so, when we eat
their muscles,

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.200
we can also take in some
creatine through our diet.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.720
(It was named after kreas
the Greek word for “meat,”

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.720
in which it was first isolated.)

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.640
We need about two grams a day;

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.960
so, those who eat meat may get
like one gram from their diet,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.240
and their body makes
the rest from scratch.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:05.400
There are rare birth defects
where you’re born

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.080
without the ability to make it,

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.120
in which case you have to get it
all externally through diet.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.880
But otherwise, our bodies can make
as much as we need to maintain

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:15.000
normal concentrations
in our muscles.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.380
When people cut out meat,
the amount of creatine floating around

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.280
in their bloodstream
goes down,

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.760
but the amount in your brain
remains the same,

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:25.120
because your brain just makes
all the creatine it needs.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:28.320
The level in vegetarian muscles
is lower,

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:30.680
but that doesn’t seem
to affect performance,

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:33.800
as both vegetarians and meat-eaters
respond to creatine supplementation

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:36.760
with similar increases
in muscle power output.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:39.280
And if vegetarian muscle creatine
was insufficient,

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.760
then presumably they would have seen
an even bigger boost.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:45.560
So basically, when you eat meat,
that just means your body

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.560
doesn’t have to make as much.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:50.960
If creatine muscle content
dropped as we grew older,

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:53.320
that might help explain
age-related muscle loss,

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:56.200
but that doesn’t seem
to be the case.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:59.160
Biopsies taken from the muscles
of young and old adults

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.800
show no difference
in creatine content.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:05.360
Still, if it improves performance,
maybe it would help.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:08.360
According to the International
Society of Sports Nutrition,

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:12.640
creatine monohydrate is the single most
effective ergogenic supplement

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:15.320
available to athletes
for increasing exercise capacity

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.760
and lean body mass
during training.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:21.520
It’s no wonder surveys show
as many as 70+ percent

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:24.280
of collegiate athletes
have used creatine supplements.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:27.560
What can it do for older adults?

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:30.080
Without exercise? Nothing.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:33.880
Most studies on creatine supplementation
alone show no benefits

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:35.960
for muscle mass, strength,
or performance.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:38.960
This makes sense,
given the mechanism.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:42.640
Creatine supplementation
delays muscle fatigue.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:45.080
This enables people to work out
longer and harder,

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:47.880
and it’s that additional
volume and intensity

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.680
that leads to the muscle benefits.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.680
So, creatine alone doesn’t help,

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:54.800
and creatine taken in the context
of the same training

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:57.760
that’s carefully controlled
and deliberately equalized

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.040
doesn’t help either.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.280
But let people exercise
as much as they can,

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.280
and most studies on creatine
supplementation

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.400
for the prevention
and treatment of sarcopenia

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:09.560
(meaning age-related muscle loss)
show augmented lean mass,

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.560
as it does in young adults.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.000
Adding three to five grams
of creatine a day

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.680
to two to three days
of resistance training a week

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:19.480
added an additional three
extra pounds of lean mass

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:22.040
over an average duration
of about four months.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:25.880
Now, some of that lean mass
may be water weight, not muscle.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:29.400
Creatine causes water retention
that can show up as lean mass,

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:32.600
but compared to placebo, creatine
combined with resistance exercise

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:35.080
increases muscle strength as well.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.520
And the additional gains in mass
and strength can persist

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:41.160
as long as 12 weeks after stopping
the creatine in older adults,

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:43.000
as long as the resistance
training is maintained,

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.960
so obviously, it’s not all
just water weight.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:49.720
A reason I never advocated for creatine
supplementation in older adults

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:52.760
for muscle preservation
was because systematic reviews

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:56.400
up through 2017 concluded
that adding creatine to training

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.680
shows mixed results
for muscle mass and strength,

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:03.760
and it did not appear to translate
to improved functioning.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:07.480
However, an updated meta-analysis
found a significant improvement

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.680
over placebo in sit-to-stand
test performance,

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:14.120
which is a decent predictor
of reduced falls risk.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:17.480
Again, this was mostly only
when accompanied by strength training.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.960
There have still been no consistent
benefits discovered

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:22.080
for just supplementing
with creatine alone.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:23.880
So, creatine should always
be prescribed

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:27.040
with a progressive strength
training regimen.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:30.160
The Society for Sarcopenia,
Cachexia, and Wasting Disease

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:34.080
convened an expert panel that,
despite the lack of long-term trials,

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:39.520
suggested creatine be indeed used
for the management of sarcopenia.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:44.440
The recommended dose to achieve
muscle saturation is 3 grams a day.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:46.760
Within a month at that slow
steady rate you achieve

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:48.280
the same muscle
levels as loading

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:51.200
with 120 grams over
a period of a week.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.960
Note, though,
it takes at least 12 weeks

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:55.160
of creatine-supplemented
resistance training

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:58.240
to see a significant
additive effect.

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:01.000
Recent evidence suggests
taking it after exercise

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.040
might be slightly
preferable to before,

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:05.400
but this has yet to be verified.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:12.080
Are there any side effects?
We’ll find out next.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:15.280
The Society for Sarcopenia,
Cachexia, and Wasting Disease

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:18.640
convened an expert panel that,
despite the lack of long-term trials,

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:22.800
suggested creatine be used for the
management of age-related muscle loss,

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.400
also known as sarcopenia.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.560
Are there any creatine side effects?

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:32.240
Well, if one can extrapolate from mice,
one side effect may be longevity.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:34.440
The average healthy lifespan
of creatine-fed mice

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:37.080
was found to be 9 percent
more than control mice,

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:39.680
and they performed better
on neurobehavioral tests,

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:41.920
especially improved memory skills.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:44.760
But is taking creatine safe?

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:48.640
One can take a bit of comfort in the fact
that it’s one of the world’s best-selling

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:52.120
dietary supplements, with literally
billions of servings taken,

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:55.680
and the only consistently reported
side effect has been weight gain,

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:57.760
presumed to be from water retention.

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:01.560
The only serious side-effects appear
to be among those with pre-existing

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:06.720
kidney diseases taking whopping doses
of like 20 grams a day for weeks.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.760
The bottom line, according
to the European Food Safety Authority,

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:14.520
is that doses of up 3 grams a day
are unlikely to pose any risk

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:18.560
“provided high purity
creatine is used.”

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:21.120
Dietary supplements
are not regulated by the FDA

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:24.000
and may not actually contain
what’s on the label

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:27.000
or, in the case of creatine,
be tainted with contaminants

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.400
generated during the industrial
production process.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:33.120
When researchers looked at 33 samples
of creatine supplements

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:37.160
made in the U.S. and Europe,
they all did actually contain creatine.

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:40.920
That’s good. But half exceeded
the maximum level recommended

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:44.120
by food safety authorities
for at least one contaminant.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:47.200
The researchers recommend that consumers
choose products from producers

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:53.440
that ensure the “highest quality control,”
but that’s easier said than done.

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:57.240
One third party supplement testing outfit
that tested for purities

00:06:57.240 --> 00:07:01.120
chose BulkSupplements brand
as their top pick,

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:05.040
which also happened to be the cheapest
at about 10 cents per daily 5 gram serving,

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:06.760
which is a level teaspoon.

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:08.800
What about just getting it from meat?

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:12.120
You could get those 3 grams of creatine
eating about five steaks a day,

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:14.640
since cooking destroys about 20 percent.

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:17.680
But the heat reacts with the creatine
and amino acids in meat

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:20.960
to create carcinogenic
heterocyclic amines,

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:24.840
one of the reasons meat
is considered to be cancer-causing.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:28.320
A separate safety concern was raised
that creatine in supplement form

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:30.520
could potentially form
a different carcinogen

00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:32.400
known as N-nitrososarcosine

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:34.640
when it hit the acid bath
of the stomach,

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:39.000
but when actually put to the test this
does not appear to be a problem.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:43.400
Some have argued caution for creatine use
among those with kidney issues.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:47.680
This concern appears to derive
in part from a misinterpretation

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.480
of laboratory data.

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:53.480
The blood levels of a different
compound called creatinine

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:55.880
is used as a marker
of kidney function.

00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:57.680
It's a muscle metabolism waste product

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:00.440
that is regularly cleared out
by well-functioning kidneys;

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:03.960
so, if your levels rise, maybe
your kidneys aren’t doing so good.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:07.800
But where does creatinine come from?
The breakdown of creatine.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:10.840
So, if you take extra creatine,
your creatinine levels in your blood

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:14.880
could rise, giving the false impression
that your kidneys are malfunctioning,

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:19.280
but instead you’re just making more,
rather than clearing less.

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:23.480
For patients who take creatine, doctors
can consider other kidney function tests

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:26.320
such as blood levels
of cystatin C levels,

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:30.000
a waste product that's more independent
of dietary intervention.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.400
So, tell your healthcare professional
if you start creatine.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:37.240
Overall, creatine supplementation
appears to be safe for the kidneys,

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.720
but the longest study to date
is less than three years;

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:43.760
so, true long-term
studies are lacking.

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:44.880
Finally today,

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:49.240
what are the potential consequences of
having to make your own creatine

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:52.320
rather than relying
on dietary sources?

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:56.920
Almost universally, research findings
show a poor vitamin B12 status

00:08:56.920 --> 00:09:01.600
among vegetarians because they're
not taking vitamin B12 supplements

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:05.720
like they should. And this results in
an elevation of homocysteine levels

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:09.160
that may explain why vegetarians
were recently found to have

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:11.280
higher rates of stroke.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:16.080
Of course, plant-based eating is just
one of many ways to get B12 deficient.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:23.680
I mean, even laughing gas can
do it, in as short as two days,

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:28.200
thanks to the recreational use
of whipped cream canister gas.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:33.400
That's something new I learned today.
Anyways, if you do eat plant-based,

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:37.160
giving vegetarians and vegans
even as little as 50 micrograms

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:40.360
once a day of cyanocobalamin, the
recommended, most stable form

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:42.800
of vitamin B12 supplement,
and their homocysteine

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:47.320
levels start up in the elevated
zone, and within 1 to 2 months

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:52.440
their homocysteines normalize right
down into the safe zone under 10.

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:57.040
Or just 2000 micrograms of
cyanocobalamin once a week,

00:09:57.040 --> 00:10:01.760
and you get the same beautiful
result, but not always.

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:06.800
In this study even 500 micrograms
a day, either as a sublingual chewable

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:09.520
or swallowable regular B12 supplement,

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:12.960
didn't normalize homocysteine
within a month. Now, presumably

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.960
if they had kept it up, their levels
would have continued to fall

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:19.320
like in the other study. But if you're
plant-based and have been taking

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:23.520
your B12 and your homocysteine levels
are still too high, meaning above 10,

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:26.600
is there anything else you can do?

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:30.120
Now, inadequate folate intake
can also increase homocysteine,

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:33.280
but folate comes from
the same root as foliage.

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:37.280
It's found in leaves, concentrated
in greens, as well as beans.

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:40.760
But if you're eating beans and
greens, taking your B12,

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:45.840
and your homocysteine level is still
too high, then I'd suggest trying,

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:50.280
as an experiment, taking
one gram of creatine a day

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:56.200
and getting your homocysteine levels
retested in a month to see if it helped.

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:59.960
Creatine is a compound formed
naturally in the human body

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:03.400
that is primarily involved in energy
production in our muscles and brain.

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:06.360
It's also naturally formed in the
bodies of many animals we eat.

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:10.520
And so when we eat their
muscles, we also can take in

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:12.160
some creatine through our diet.

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:15.520
We need about two grams a day,
so those who eat meat may get

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:19.720
like one gram from their diet, and
their body makes the rest from scratch.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:23.760
There are rare birth defects where
you're born without the ability to make it,

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:26.480
in which case you have to get it
from your diet, but otherwise

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:29.200
our bodies make as
much as we need

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:32.240
to maintain normal
concentrations in our muscles.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:35.680
When you cut out meat, the
amount of creatine floating around

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:40.400
in your bloodstream goes down, but the
amount in your brain remains the same,

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:45.280
showing dietary creatine doesn't
influence the levels of brain creatine,

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:48.560
because your brain just makes
all the creatine you need.

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:52.880
The level in vegetarian muscles is
lower, but that doesn't seem to affect

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:55.960
performance, as both vegetarians
and meat-eaters respond

00:11:55.960 --> 00:12:00.080
to creatine supplementation with similar
increases in muscle power output.

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:02.760
And if vegetarian muscle
creatine was insufficient,

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:05.920
then presumably they would
have seen an even bigger boost.

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:08.920
So basically, all that happens
when you eat meat

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:12.440
is that your body just doesn't
have to make as much.

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:15.520
What does this all have
to do with homocysteine?

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:19.480
Okay, in the process of making creatine,
your body produces homocysteine

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:22.440
as a waste product. Now
normally this isn't a problem

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:25.480
because your body
has two ways to detoxify it

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:30.240
using vitamin B6 or using a
combination of vitamins B12 and folate.

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:34.720
Now B6 is found in both plant and
animal foods; it's rare to be deficient.

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:38.200
But B12 is mainly in animal
foods, and so can be too low

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:42.320
in those eating plant-based who don't
supplement or eat B12 fortified foods.

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:46.000
And folate is concentrated in plant
foods, so can be low in those

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:49.440
who don't regularly eat greens or
beans or folic-acid fortified grains,

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:54.880
and without that escape valve
homocysteine levels can get too high.

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:58.280
If, however, you're eating a healthy
plant-based diet and taking your B12

00:12:58.280 --> 00:13:02.360
supplement, your homocysteine levels
should be fine, but what if they're not?

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:06.320
One might predict that if you started
taking creatine supplements,

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:09.640
the level of homocysteine might go
down since you're not going to have

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:16.153
to be making so much of it from scratch,
producing homocysteine as a by-product.

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:18.480
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:21.600
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:24.080
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:28.520
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:33.840
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
images, or studies mentioned here,

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:36.360
go to the Nutrition Facts
Podcast landing page.

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:38.780
There you’ll find all the
